      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Mountain Brook House, built 1832, served as an inn and tavern, later the Gin Point Inn and Hyde‑Away restaurant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/middleville_new_jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Middleville sits at the confluence of Stillwater Road, West Shore Drive, and Pond Brook Road along Trout Brook, a tributary of the Paulins Kill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/middleville_new_jersey",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community lies 5.8 miles west of Newton, within the Skylands Region, and rises to 525 feet above sea level.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
